  "contribution": {
    "summary": "Qualify M3-W01-C02-T2 with a controlled RED, 19 independent numerical GREEN tests, full Math regressions, explicit nearest-even rational-to-binary64 conversion and typed precision-loss, underflow, overflow and budget outcomes. Verify copy-only matrices and local provider-neutral NuGet 0.4.0-preview.2; complete C02 without closing M3.",
    "value": "A qualified consumer can choose exact-only or admitted approximate binary64 matrix conversion and inspect typed errors without silent rational widening, partial results, aliases, or dependencies on a specific numerical provider.",
    "debtChanges": [
      "Discovery remains a separate proposed M3-W03 work package; it cannot claim native DWF adoption before Workflow issue 139 authoring and sibling-continuation support are qualified and installed.",
      "The neutral dw.discovery project under aihallot/dw.tools remains at the independent planning/adoption stage; this numerical run neither duplicates its contract nor publishes a Math agent skill.",
      "No native BLAS, untested operating-system RID, external provider availability, AURA authorization or Decision adoption is inferred from the local managed package check.",
      "IEEE 754 nearest-even reporting is mathematically exact for bounded rational operands, but a rounded value does not become exact algebraic equality or certify downstream solver conditioning.",
      "Verify the 4096-bit operand boundary through actual conversion outcomes (4096 bits accepted for evaluation, 4097 bits refused), not a tautological constant assertion (MSTEST0032). Underflow, overflow and bit-budget refusals never yield a partial matrix.",
      "Closing M3-W01-C02 does not complete M3-W01 or M3; the next planned numerical chunk is M3-W01-C03 for solving and decompositions."
    ],
    "nextAction": "After durable RS041 success, prepare a substantive M3-W01-C03 numerical solve and decomposition slice under the existing native DWF plan, while monitoring the separate generic dw.discovery and Workflow issue 139 gates.",
    "achievements": [
      {
        "projectNode": "M3-W01-C02-T2-R",
        "achievement": "Compiled independent numerical-test assembly observes missing rational-to-binary64 public result contract before its source is installed; retain the exact controlled RED evidence."
      },
      {
        "projectNode": "M3-W01-C02-T2-G",
        "achievement": "Implement correctly rounded bounded BigInteger-rational to finite IEEE binary64 conversion with exact absolute error, explicit rounding policies and no implicit widening or partial matrices."
      },
      {
        "projectNode": "M3-W01-C02-T2-V",
        "achievement": "Nineteen independent numerical GREEN oracles, recovered RED, full Math regressions, copy/alias checks and local provider-free NuGet 0.4.0-preview.2 manifest pass."
      },
      {
        "projectNode": "M3-W01-C02-T2",
        "achievement": "Qualify declared exact-versus-approximate conversion, loss reporting and provider-load boundaries without changing third-party numerical packages or claiming external consumers."
      },
      {
        "projectNode": "M3-W01-C02",
        "achievement": "Both accepted numerical matrix/vector tasks T1 and T2 are done with durable evidence; M3 and its numerical work package remain in progress for solving and decompositions."
      }
    ]
  },
